# AgriSaarthi 360 — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local development. NEVER commit real keys.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini — server-side only.
# The browser never sees these values; they are read only inside
# lib/crop-health/vision-provider.ts and lib/assistant/gemini-provider.ts
# via Next.js API routes.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a free key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Leave empty to run the deterministic fallbacks instead.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# Crop health — vision-capable Flash model.
# If absent, the code defaults to a current Flash model.
GEMINI_VISION_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# Assistant — text-capable Flash model.
# If absent, the code defaults to a current Flash model.
GEMINI_ASSISTANT_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# P1 PROVENANCE (optional — default is honest local verification, no chain)
# The app fully functions without these: the timeline shows
# "Local verification" instead of blockchain verification.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROVENANCE_ADAPTER=local|testnet  (default: local)
# PROVENANCE_CHAIN=polygon-amoy
# PROVENANCE_NETWORK=amoy
# PROVENANCE_RPC_ENDPOINT=https://...
# PROVENANCE_API_KEY=...
# PROVENANCE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=0x...  (a real deployed TESTNET contract only — never hard-coded in source)
#
# BLOCKCHAIN ANCHORING (testnet only — see docs/blockchain/README.md):
# With PROVENANCE_ADAPTER=testnet AND the variables above set AND a
# signer below, the timeline gains an explicit "Anchor on Testnet"
# action: the canonical record hash (bytes32 only — never farm data) is
# committed through the minimal ProvenanceAnchor contract and verified
# on-chain. Without it, records stay LOCAL VERIFIED.
# PROVENANCE_PRIVATE_KEY=your_private_key_here   # SERVER ONLY — never commit; use a throwaway testnet wallet

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weather uses keyless Open-Meteo — no configuration required.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
